\description{
Construct and manipulate a \link[=fleet-class]{fleet} object defining the exploitation
characteristics of a fleet for a stock in an operating model.
}
\details{
A \link[=fleet-class]{fleet} object describes the fishing characteristics of a fleet for
a particular stock in an operating model, including effort dynamics,
catchability, selectivity, retention, discard mortality, and spatial
closures.
\subsection{Required and Optional Components}{

\code{\link[=Selectivity]{Selectivity()}} and \code{\link[=Effort]{Effort()}} are required for all fleets. All other
components are optional and will use default values if not specified:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=Catchability]{Catchability()}}: defaults to efficiency = 1 across all years.
\item \code{\link[=Retention]{Retention()}}: defaults to full retention for all age and length classes.
\item \code{\link[=DiscardMortality]{DiscardMortality()}}: defaults to 0 (all discards survive).
\item \code{Closure}: defaults to 1 (all areas open) across all simulations and years.
\item \code{WeightFleetRetained}/\code{WeightFleetSelected}: computed from selectivity,
retention, and the stock's weight-at-length.
}
}

\subsection{Pass-Through Access from an OM}{

When \code{Name} is an \link[=om-class]{om} object, \code{Fleet()} acts as an accessor rather
than a constructor:
\itemize{
\item \code{Fleet(om)} returns the full fleet list (\code{om@Fleet}).
\item \code{Fleet(om, st)} returns all fleets for stock index \code{st}
(\code{om@Fleet[[st]]}), where \code{st} is passed via the \code{Effort} argument.
\item \code{Fleet(om, st, fl)} returns fleet \code{fl} for stock \code{st}
(\code{om@Fleet[[st]][[fl]]}), where \code{fl} is passed via the \code{Catchability}
argument.
}
}

\subsection{Assigning Fleets to an OM}{

\code{\link[=Stock]{Stock()}} objects must be added to the OM before fleets. A single
\link[=fleet-class]{fleet} object assigned with \code{Fleet(om) <- MyFleet} is applied to all
stocks using the fleet name. A list must be structured as a stock-indexed
list of fleet lists.
}

\subsection{Bookkeeping Slots}{

The slots \code{nYear}, \code{pYear}, \code{nSim}, \code{CurrentYear}, \code{Years}, and \code{Seasons}
are inherited from the paired \link[=stock-class]{stock} object automatically when
\code{\link[=PopulateFleet]{PopulateFleet()}} is called and do not need to be set manually.
}

\subsection{Closure Array}{

\code{Closure} has dimensions \verb{Sim x Year x Area}. The \code{Sim} and \code{Year}
dimensions may be length 1 (replicated internally by \code{\link[=PopulateClosure]{PopulateClosure()}}).
If the array is empty or \code{NULL}, all areas are set to open (1) across all
simulations and years. Dimension names for \code{Sim}, \code{Year}, and \code{Area} are
added automatically if missing.

Individual slots may be accessed or modified using \code{\link[=Effort]{Effort()}},
\code{\link[=Catchability]{Catchability()}}, \code{\link[=Selectivity]{Selectivity()}}, \code{\link[=Retention]{Retention()}}, \code{\link[=DiscardMortality]{DiscardMortality()}},
\code{\link[=Closure]{Closure()}}, \code{\link[=WeightFleetRetained]{WeightFleetRetained()}}, \code{\link[=WeightFleetSelected]{WeightFleetSelected()}}, and
\code{\link[=Bioeconomic]{Bioeconomic()}}.
}
}
\examples{
## ---- Minimal Fleet object ----
# Effort and Selectivity are required. All other components use defaults:
# Catchability = 1, Retention = full, DiscardMortality = 0,
# Closure = all open, WeightFleet = stock weight-at-age.
eff <- Effort(Effort = data.frame(
  Year  = c(2000, 2010, 2024),
  Lower = c(0,    0.5,  1),
  Upper = c(0,    0.7,  1),
  CV    = c(0.1,  0.1,  0.1)
))
sel <- Selectivity(Pars = list(L5 = 20, LFS = 35, Vmaxlen = 1))

f <- Fleet(Name = "Trawl", Effort = eff, Selectivity = sel)
f

## ---- Fleet with all components specified ----
f_full <- Fleet(
  Name             = "Trawl",
  Effort           = eff,
  Catchability     = Catchability(Efficiency = 0.01),
  Selectivity      = sel,
  Retention        = Retention(Pars = list(LR5 = 15, LFR = 28, Rmaxlen = 1)),
  DiscardMortality = DiscardMortality(MeanAtAge = 0.2)
)
f_full

## ---- Closure: partial spatio-temporal closure ----
# Closure has dimensions Sim x Year x Area (Sim/Year may be length 1 and are
# replicated internally). 1 = open, 0 = closed.
# Here area 3 is closed from 2010 onwards; areas 1 and 2 are always open.
years <- 2000:2024
closure_array <- array(1, dim = c(1, length(years), 3),
                       dimnames = list(Sim = 1, Year = years, Area = 1:3))
closure_array[1, as.character(2010:2024), 3] <- 0

f_closure <- Fleet(Name = "Trawl", Effort = eff, Selectivity = sel,
                    Closure = closure_array)
Closure(f_closure)

## ---- Slot accessors and replacement ----
Effort(f_full)
Catchability(f_full)
Selectivity(f_full)
Retention(f_full)
DiscardMortality(f_full)
WeightFleet(f_full)

Selectivity(f_full)   <- Selectivity(Pars = list(L5 = 25, LFS = 40, Vmaxlen = 0.8))
Catchability(f_full)  <- Catchability(Efficiency = 0.02)

## ---- Assigning fleets to an OM ----
# Stock objects must be added to the OM before fleets.
stock1 <- Stock(Name = "Snapper")
stock2 <- Stock(Name = "Grouper")
om <- OM()
Stock(om) <- list(Snapper = stock1, Grouper = stock2)

# A single Fleet applied to all stocks by name
Fleet(om) <- f
Fleet(om)

# A stock-indexed list of fleets: stock -> fleet -> Fleet object
longline <- Fleet(Name = "Longline", Effort = eff,
                   Selectivity = Selectivity(Pars = list(SA50 = 4, SA50_95 = 2)))
Fleet(om) <- list(Snapper = list(Trawl = f), Grouper = list(Longline = longline))
Fleet(om)

## ---- Pass-through access from an OM ----
Fleet(om)        # full fleet list
Fleet(om, 1)     # all fleets for stock index 1 (Snapper)
Fleet(om, 2, 1)  # fleet index 1 for stock index 2 (Grouper -> Longline)
}
